<i>For me, your assessment and the conversation as a whole were very therapeutic. You pinpointed the main problems of the projects in my portfolio very accurately; it was like an instant reality check, and the real state of things became clear.</i>
<div class="ids__space S"></div>
<i>What’s really nice is that we ended on a positive note — some of your comments genuinely motivated me. We had just talked about design having to relate to real things, and cut to: I’m redesigning the bill for building repairs that annoyed me this morning.</i>
