<i>After the meeting things are going well: I got energy and an understanding of what to do next. It really perked me up.</i>
<div class="ids__space S"></div>
<i>The thing is, with reviews from fellow designers and friends there’s little chance of getting an honest answer. Everyone says nice things, you’re great — and here it’s great that an unbiased pro can say what they think without fear of offending you.</i>
<div class="ids__space S"></div>
<i>I really liked this experience, and I was especially glad about the pay-what-you-want price, because things like this can be very hard to sign up for when they’re expensive.</i>
<div class="ids__space S"></div>
<i>Of the things that could be improved, I’ll name only one, and it’s not critical. Honest and sincere reactions are very necessary and important to me, but in the first second, when I heard “well, this is fucked up”, I got a little scared. Then I realized you weren’t going to scold me — it was just a way of expressing emotion.</i>
<div class="ids__space S"></div>
<i>It was also really great that you share knowledge about how the market works now. It’s great to hear this from people immersed in the industry; you want to believe it, and it helps you get your bearings</i>
